WEBVTT

00:17.308 --> 00:19.269
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

00:19.352 --> 00:20.186
Thank you.

00:20.270 --> 00:23.648
Up 'til now, I was confident I
could talk to pretty much anyone.

00:24.149 --> 00:25.150
Minato.

00:25.233 --> 00:26.901
- Minato.
- Minato.

00:26.985 --> 00:28.695
- But...
- Oh, Hikawa.

00:29.738 --> 00:31.281
Whenever I talk to her...

00:31.364 --> 00:32.949
I always feel so awkward.

00:33.450 --> 00:35.368
We just finished morning practice.

00:36.202 --> 00:38.121
Is there anything we can talk about?

00:38.747 --> 00:41.583
Oh, by the way, Igarashi was here
yesterday...

00:41.666 --> 00:42.751
Whoa, her face...

00:43.251 --> 00:44.961
Was that a sore subject?

00:46.212 --> 00:48.089
Yeah, they definitely don't seem close.

00:48.173 --> 00:50.550
And Igarashi came across as pretty
intense.

00:51.718 --> 00:53.094
Maybe she doesn't like him.

00:53.887 --> 00:54.888
I messed up.

00:55.388 --> 00:59.350
Maybe junior high was always off-limits
and I should've never even brought it up.

00:59.434 --> 01:00.894
Nice job, Minato.

01:01.936 --> 01:02.979
Oh, I'm sorry.

01:03.480 --> 01:05.899
We should just stop talking about
junior high.

01:07.484 --> 01:10.153
Jeez, could I have phrased that any
more awkwardly?

01:10.779 --> 01:12.906
Man, I'm really crashing and
burning here.

01:13.782 --> 01:16.785
The more I talk, the deeper I dig
myself into a hole.

01:17.744 --> 01:18.578
Wait...

01:19.162 --> 01:20.997
Have I always been like this?

01:27.337 --> 01:29.047
Ah, the cold air feels so good.

01:31.508 --> 01:33.927
- Koyun.
- Why do you have to be such a busybody?

01:37.180 --> 01:38.264
I don't get it.

01:39.474 --> 01:41.226
The sound of the door locking...

01:41.726 --> 01:42.811
It makes me sick.

01:44.646 --> 01:45.897
I think I heard it.

01:50.485 --> 01:52.237
Did Koyun just... Hold on.

01:52.737 --> 01:54.072
What just happened?

01:54.155 --> 01:56.199
Aw, man. I think...

01:56.699 --> 01:59.202
Don't try to put the moves on her
or be weird!

02:00.245 --> 02:01.788
Miki's totally gonna kill me.

02:04.374 --> 02:05.208
Huh?

03:37.133 --> 03:39.135
Change

03:41.012 --> 03:43.389
SCHOOL NURSE'S OFFICE

03:43.473 --> 03:45.934
- GLOOM
- Oh, come on!

03:46.684 --> 03:48.228
Are you just eating a sweet bun for lunch

03:48.311 --> 03:49.437
again?

03:49.979 --> 03:50.813
Noriko.

03:51.439 --> 03:54.150
Is there any way to keep yourself
from getting mad?

03:54.234 --> 03:55.610
Wow, I didn't think that you ever

03:55.693 --> 03:57.570
- got mad!
- It's so hot. It's so cold.

03:58.988 --> 04:00.031
Were you in a fight?

04:00.114 --> 04:01.157
Uh... Mm...

04:02.742 --> 04:03.576
Well...

04:03.660 --> 04:07.413
It's natural to get angry from time to
time, and it's important to not keep

04:07.497 --> 04:08.581
bottling it up.

04:09.082 --> 04:10.083
Hmm.

04:10.750 --> 04:14.420
I wish I could just take it out
on someone else to make me feel better.

04:14.504 --> 04:17.548
But I'm just not the type of person
who can do that.

04:18.466 --> 04:20.385
I know that much about myself.

04:21.844 --> 04:24.973
If anything, I just end up regretting
whatever I said.

04:25.056 --> 04:25.974
SELF-LOATHING

04:26.057 --> 04:27.225
You're a difficult one.

04:28.142 --> 04:31.354
I don't know what happened, but if
you're upset, it's best to communicate

04:31.437 --> 04:33.439
your feelings to the other person.

04:33.523 --> 04:35.858
If you don't like something, then just
say that.

04:35.942 --> 04:36.859
Communicate...

04:37.777 --> 04:38.653
I didn't do that.

04:39.612 --> 04:40.488
In that moment...

04:41.030 --> 04:42.740
I was just so upset...

04:43.533 --> 04:44.575
It makes me sick.

04:45.451 --> 04:46.911
I intentionally hurt him.

04:47.870 --> 04:52.083
And I did it without even hearing
Amamiya out or explaining myself.

04:53.293 --> 04:54.585
I'm still frustrated.

04:55.086 --> 04:58.339
And now pile onto it, the regret
over what I said to him.

05:01.718 --> 05:03.386
- I just want some peace and quiet.
- Sigh.

05:03.469 --> 05:06.014
Stop sounding like an old fart, and be a
teenager.

05:07.932 --> 05:08.850
Oh, there you are.

05:10.727 --> 05:11.561
Hey, Koyun.

05:12.061 --> 05:13.688
I'm gonna eat my lunch here too.

05:14.314 --> 05:16.566
I already told you, this isn't
a cafeteria.

05:17.066 --> 05:18.443
Do you want any of this?

05:18.526 --> 05:19.444
No, thanks.

05:19.527 --> 05:20.528
Seriously?

05:21.029 --> 05:22.739
Is something wrong?

05:22.822 --> 05:25.283
Just wanted to check in and see how
you were.

05:25.366 --> 05:26.326
This morning...

05:26.826 --> 05:28.369
I caught your conversation...

05:28.870 --> 05:30.163
with Minato.

05:30.246 --> 05:31.080
Ugh.

05:38.838 --> 05:41.424
Just clean up after yourselves before you
leave.

05:41.507 --> 05:43.217
- Okay.
- Okay.

05:44.635 --> 05:45.595
NURSE IS MAKING ROUNDS

05:45.678 --> 05:46.512
So, look, Koyun...

05:47.555 --> 05:49.057
Minato tends to...

05:51.517 --> 05:53.019
ego, is kinda childish, and can be

05:53.102 --> 05:53.394
Hey, w-wait a minute.

05:53.478 --> 05:54.312
Get too close, oversteps, has a big

05:54.395 --> 05:57.273
- ego, is kinda childish, and can be
- Hey, w-wait a minute.

05:57.357 --> 05:59.275
But he's not a bad guy, I promise you.

06:00.860 --> 06:03.154
And I hope this doesn't come across
weird...

06:03.237 --> 06:06.824
But Minato and I actually knew
of you since back in junior high.

06:07.450 --> 06:08.284
What?

06:09.118 --> 06:10.828
We didn't know your name...

06:11.329 --> 06:14.832
But the other day, when you said you
were on the basketball team, I put it

06:14.916 --> 06:16.959
- together.
- Basketball.

06:17.460 --> 06:19.670
- Does that mean...
- Mm-hm.

06:20.713 --> 06:22.507
Miki let us know what happened.

06:22.590 --> 06:25.343
She told us about how you were being
bullied back then.

06:28.554 --> 06:30.014
- Good morning, Koyun!
- Hm?

06:30.598 --> 06:33.768
I got here with time to spare, which
never happens so...

06:35.853 --> 06:36.687
Huh?

06:37.230 --> 06:39.148
What the... Who would...?

06:39.232 --> 06:40.566
Don't worry about it.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.693
What do you mean, "Don't worry about it?"

06:42.777 --> 06:43.778
How long has...?

06:43.861 --> 06:44.946
I can't remember.

06:45.446 --> 06:46.531
Since forever?

06:49.117 --> 06:50.993
I hope it all ends soon.

06:52.662 --> 06:55.540
So Miki told you guys what happened
back then.

06:55.623 --> 06:57.375
Yeah, but don't get mad at her.

06:57.875 --> 07:01.129
It was just because she was
really worried about you at the time.

07:01.212 --> 07:02.922
Yeah... I know.

07:03.005 --> 07:04.382
Miki also said...

07:05.091 --> 07:07.468
She didn't realize her friend was
struggling.

07:07.969 --> 07:10.263
And that she had no idea how to help you.

07:10.763 --> 07:14.016
I wondered why she never told me about
what was going on.

07:14.100 --> 07:17.478
Maybe she felt as though she couldn't
trust me.

07:18.146 --> 07:20.106
It all just makes me so sad.

07:20.648 --> 07:21.899
You're not untrustworthy.

07:21.983 --> 07:24.819
Maybe she just didn't wanna bother
you or worry you.

07:24.902 --> 07:26.446
And nothing more than that.

07:27.155 --> 07:29.365
Do you really think that's what it is?

07:29.449 --> 07:30.450
UGH, UGH, UGH

07:30.533 --> 07:31.826
I don't want her holding back just to
spare my feelings.

07:31.909 --> 07:33.202
Whoa, hey, calm down.

07:34.162 --> 07:37.206
- So. yeah...
- I had no idea she felt that way.

07:38.541 --> 07:40.585
The reason I didn't talk to her about it...

07:40.668 --> 07:42.128
Go for it, Miki!

07:43.880 --> 07:45.965
- Nice!
- That was awesome!

07:46.048 --> 07:48.885
Was because she was so dedicated to
her club activities.

07:48.968 --> 07:54.056
Whereas I only kept showing up to them
because I was too afraid to quit.

07:54.599 --> 07:55.725
We were opposites.

07:56.893 --> 07:57.727
So, no.

07:57.810 --> 08:00.980
I never though she was unreliable
or that I couldn't trust her.

08:02.690 --> 08:03.524
Hmm.

08:04.567 --> 08:08.237
And seeing how you and Miki interact,
I guess Minato might've also picked

08:08.321 --> 08:09.155
up on it by now.

08:09.238 --> 08:12.200
That you and her were old friends from
the basketball team.

08:12.283 --> 08:13.117
Oh.

08:13.201 --> 08:15.912
So that's probably why Minato was
concerned about you.

08:15.995 --> 08:16.829
That's all.

08:17.788 --> 08:18.623
That's why.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.083
Oh... I'm sorry.

08:21.626 --> 08:23.544
Let's stop talking about junior high.

08:24.504 --> 08:26.547
That's why Amamiya said what he said.

08:27.965 --> 08:31.427
And I completely took it the wrong
way and said all those awful things to

08:31.511 --> 08:32.345
him.

08:33.387 --> 08:35.056
H-How embarrassing.

08:35.139 --> 08:36.057
Are you okay?

08:37.099 --> 08:39.977
Not at all.
I must offer an apology right away.

08:40.478 --> 08:42.647
That sounds so... uh, formal.

08:43.231 --> 08:44.899
Want me to just tell him for you?

08:44.982 --> 08:45.942
No.

08:46.025 --> 08:47.735
I must express the apology.

08:47.818 --> 08:48.819
What?

08:49.862 --> 08:52.698
I'm telling you, it probably didn't
bother him at all.

08:53.199 --> 08:54.408
It's fine, don't worry.

08:54.492 --> 08:55.701
It's Minato.

08:56.786 --> 08:58.287
Hey, Amamiya!

09:00.206 --> 09:01.541
Hey, sorry, my bad.

09:01.624 --> 09:02.458
Over here!

09:04.252 --> 09:06.295
Hey. Hey, d'you hear me?

09:06.379 --> 09:08.631
Whoa! Yo, what's up?

09:09.340 --> 09:11.092
Are you mad or s- something?

09:12.260 --> 09:14.136
Sorry, I wasn't paying attention.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.388
Uh. Oh.

09:16.514 --> 09:17.598
Dude, you scared me.

09:17.682 --> 09:19.392
I thought you were mad at me.

09:19.475 --> 09:23.062
No, dummy, he just looks intense
when he's not smiling.

09:25.815 --> 09:28.067
Why do you have to be such a busybody?

09:28.901 --> 09:33.114
Was she upset because I talked to
Igarashi or something?

09:33.948 --> 09:36.742
And why would that make her so mad?

09:37.743 --> 09:39.370
- You shouldn't do to others what you
- Nice!

09:39.453 --> 09:40.913
- Wouldn't want done to yourself, I know
- Good arm!

09:40.997 --> 09:42.039
- That.
- Thanks.

09:42.123 --> 09:44.458
- But I shouldn't do the opposite?
- My turn!

09:44.542 --> 09:46.168
- Oops.
- I don't get it.

09:47.086 --> 09:47.920
Maybe...

09:48.838 --> 09:50.256
We're just too different.

09:50.756 --> 09:52.717
In our values and ways of thinking.

09:54.468 --> 09:56.137
What might work for me...

09:57.888 --> 09:59.807
Seems to not work for her.

10:01.100 --> 10:04.020
So whatever I do, it only ends up
bothering her.

10:07.231 --> 10:11.235
Is it arrogant of me to think I should do
something for her in the first place?

10:11.319 --> 10:12.445
Is that it, Miki?

10:12.528 --> 10:13.529
Huh?

10:14.405 --> 10:17.241
But, if I'm arrogant, couldn't you
say the same for her?

10:17.867 --> 10:21.370
She draws a line between people she
likes and people she doesn't.

10:21.454 --> 10:24.457
Yota and Miki are on the side of the
people she accepts.

10:24.540 --> 10:27.043
On the other hand, I'm on the side she
writes off.

10:28.669 --> 10:29.503
UNEASY

10:29.587 --> 10:31.797
- Man, it's starting to make me angry.
- Whoa!

10:34.342 --> 10:35.926
Whoa! What's wrong?

10:36.510 --> 10:38.721
Yeah. I'll stop getting involved with her.

10:39.221 --> 10:41.182
It's not doing either of us any good.

10:41.265 --> 10:43.684
So, I won't worry about it anymore.

10:44.977 --> 10:47.855
Yota.
Where were you during the lunch break?

10:48.356 --> 10:49.565
Mmm.

10:50.232 --> 10:51.233
The bathroom?

10:51.317 --> 10:52.318
Forever.

10:56.364 --> 11:00.034
School's over now, but I never found
a good time to apologize.

11:01.035 --> 11:03.871
Is there ever really a good time
to apologize?

11:03.954 --> 11:05.081
APOLOGIZE TIMING

11:05.581 --> 11:09.168
Well, let's hope I get a chance tomorrow.

11:09.251 --> 11:10.294
See you, Minato.

11:11.087 --> 11:11.921
See ya.

11:13.839 --> 11:14.924
Oh, I, um, I mean...

11:30.940 --> 11:35.027
I'm realizing, up until now, I never made
the effort to see him for who he really

11:35.111 --> 11:35.945
is.

11:39.573 --> 11:41.784
I assumed he'd treat me like others have.

11:41.867 --> 11:44.328
So I wrote him off, just like that.

11:45.371 --> 11:47.331
Rejected him without even knowing him.

11:48.124 --> 11:52.086
I've been doing things to him that
I know I wouldn't want done to me.

11:58.884 --> 12:00.094
That face again.

12:00.720 --> 12:03.723
The one she makes around people she
keeps her guard up with.

12:04.807 --> 12:07.685
I thought maybe we could eventually
become friends.

12:08.436 --> 12:10.604
I guess that was just my ego talking.

12:11.480 --> 12:12.648
I was doing it for me.

12:13.315 --> 12:15.067
And to her, I was just annoying.

12:15.818 --> 12:18.696
Maybe it would've been better if I
hadn't gotten involved with her in the

12:18.779 --> 12:20.239
- first place.
- Amamiya!

12:21.157 --> 12:21.991
Huh?

12:24.785 --> 12:25.619
I'm sorry.

12:28.706 --> 12:31.709
I'm sorry, but can you and I... talk?

12:37.381 --> 12:38.215
Um...

12:38.799 --> 12:40.217
Do you have time right now?

12:40.718 --> 12:41.677
Yeah.

12:41.761 --> 12:43.929
My club doesn't start for a few minutes.

12:45.639 --> 12:47.516
So, about this morning...

12:48.392 --> 12:49.310
What should I do?

12:50.019 --> 12:51.228
This is so embarrassing.

12:51.771 --> 12:53.314
Everything about this is embarrassing.

12:53.397 --> 12:55.065
MISUNDERSTANDING, PARANOIA
SELF-CONSCIOUSNES

12:55.149 --> 12:55.983
Ugh.

12:56.567 --> 12:58.736
I'm sorry for saying such mean things.

12:59.528 --> 13:00.362
Sure.

13:00.446 --> 13:04.033
In the moment, I wondered why you knew
about something from when I was

13:04.116 --> 13:06.118
in junior high.

13:06.702 --> 13:10.289
I just couldn't stand the thought that
you might've heard about it from

13:10.372 --> 13:11.373
Igarashi.

13:11.874 --> 13:12.792
DOESN'T GET PERSONAL SPACE
ONLY WANTS TO HELP

13:12.875 --> 13:16.378
But, Yota told me at lunch that it was
just a misunderstanding.

13:17.087 --> 13:18.005
Yota did?

13:18.589 --> 13:19.423
Wait.

13:20.132 --> 13:20.966
Mmm.

13:21.842 --> 13:23.761
- The bathroom?
- That liar.

13:24.845 --> 13:25.763
I'm sorry, I...

13:26.722 --> 13:28.474
I misunderstood things.

13:29.225 --> 13:30.184
And I was rude.

13:30.810 --> 13:31.644
And I...

13:32.937 --> 13:33.771
I, uh...

13:34.605 --> 13:35.481
I have...

13:35.564 --> 13:37.566
I have so much I want to say.

13:38.943 --> 13:39.777
But I can never get it to come out

13:39.860 --> 13:40.694
WANT TO APOLOGIZE PROPERLY FOR WHOSE SAKE?

13:40.778 --> 13:41.654
how I want it to.

13:41.737 --> 13:42.780
SELF-SATISFACTION?
WANT TO CHANGE

13:42.863 --> 13:46.742
The more my thoughts start to pile up on
me, the more everything I try to say

13:46.826 --> 13:49.787
gets stuck in my throat.

13:51.664 --> 13:54.375
All the feelings I can't voice try to
escape as tears.

13:58.170 --> 13:59.004
Oh no!

13:59.547 --> 14:00.422
No, no, no, no!

14:00.506 --> 14:01.549
Get back in there!

14:02.049 --> 14:03.259
Oh, this always happens.

14:03.342 --> 14:05.177
The apologizer can't cry!

14:05.261 --> 14:06.470
Dry up, dry up, dry up!

14:07.137 --> 14:09.265
Hikawa.

14:09.974 --> 14:11.267
Hey, it's okay.

14:12.726 --> 14:14.854
You don't have to apologize so much.

14:14.937 --> 14:17.356
Look, if anything, I'm the one
who made you feel bad.

14:17.439 --> 14:19.942
Wait, hold on. I was just pissed
off at her a moment ago. Why am I

14:20.025 --> 14:20.860
trying to comfort her all of a sudden?

14:20.943 --> 14:23.070
Seriously, you can say whatever you
want to me, alright?

14:23.153 --> 14:24.363
Don't bottle it up. Huh?

14:25.239 --> 14:26.782
DRIP

14:27.491 --> 14:28.325
Uh?

14:28.909 --> 14:32.538
When someone's kind to me when I'm
holding my tears back, the floodgates

14:32.621 --> 14:33.664
just open and...

14:35.708 --> 14:37.209
- Oh.
- Tears?

14:39.962 --> 14:41.213
LINT, LOOSE THREADS

14:41.297 --> 14:42.256
SLIP

14:42.965 --> 14:43.799
- You know,
- Hm?

14:44.633 --> 14:48.012
I was lying when I said I didn't know
Igarashi.

14:48.596 --> 14:49.847
- Huh?
- It's the opposite.

14:51.724 --> 14:53.934
We're actually not on very good terms.

14:55.895 --> 14:57.521
Where are we taking this again?

14:58.147 --> 15:00.065
Turn left here and go straight.

15:02.401 --> 15:03.527
Tears, just the two of us...

15:03.611 --> 15:04.987
They'll get the wrong idea!

15:05.905 --> 15:06.739
Hikawa...

15:09.658 --> 15:11.785
- It's so heavy, right?
- Huh?

15:11.869 --> 15:13.329
Look at this. Look.

15:13.412 --> 15:14.330
What do you think?

15:14.872 --> 15:16.749
- Hm?
- What're they doing?

15:16.832 --> 15:19.376
Maybe they caught a rare monster
or something?

15:19.460 --> 15:21.295
Oh, my parents are really into that game.

15:21.378 --> 15:24.840
They like that you have to walk around
doing it, so you get exercise.

15:27.217 --> 15:28.302
Thank you for that.

15:31.513 --> 15:33.807
- What's that?
- Uh... Oh, um, that's...

15:34.808 --> 15:36.185
My Pomeranian.

15:38.312 --> 15:39.396
Oh, I made her laugh.

15:42.024 --> 15:43.067
It's so cute.

15:48.072 --> 15:49.323
I should get going now.

15:49.823 --> 15:50.741
Oh, sorry.

15:51.241 --> 15:52.242
Well...

15:55.287 --> 15:56.747
I'll see ya tomorrow.

15:57.289 --> 15:58.123
Yeah.

15:58.999 --> 15:59.833
See ya then.

16:15.140 --> 16:17.768
Hmm? Wait, now that I think about it...

16:18.268 --> 16:21.188
Hikawa said she and Igarashi are on bad
terms.

16:21.689 --> 16:23.232
But when I asked him...

16:23.899 --> 16:28.028
Oh, by the way, Igarashi, do you remember
Hikawa?

16:30.364 --> 16:31.198
Huh?

16:32.032 --> 16:32.908
Hikawa?

16:33.784 --> 16:36.495
Nah, there was no one by that name in our
junior high.

16:37.329 --> 16:38.163
So he said.

16:39.123 --> 16:40.541
What's going on there?

16:41.542 --> 16:42.376
Hmmm...

16:47.715 --> 16:49.550
Neither of them seem to be lying.

16:50.050 --> 16:51.135
It's the opposite.

16:51.635 --> 16:52.511
Wait, who?

16:53.012 --> 16:55.222
What happened between those two
in the past?

16:55.305 --> 16:57.641
Why do you have to be such a busybody?

16:57.725 --> 16:58.559
Ugh!

16:59.810 --> 17:00.644
Huh...

17:01.478 --> 17:03.313
Is something wrong, Amamiya?

17:03.397 --> 17:04.398
What?

17:04.481 --> 17:06.692
- No, nothing.
- Don't lie!

17:06.775 --> 17:10.362
You haven't been listening to a single
word I've been saying, have you?

17:14.199 --> 17:16.869
- What are you, his girlfriend?
- Or you sound like one.

17:16.952 --> 17:19.538
Minato, if you keep spacing out,
your noodles will get all soggy.

17:19.621 --> 17:21.957
What kind of combination is that, man?

17:22.041 --> 17:22.875
That's gross.

17:23.417 --> 17:24.293
They're delicious.

17:24.376 --> 17:25.794
Too many carbs.

17:25.878 --> 17:27.546
- Huh?
- Yota.

17:28.130 --> 17:30.674
Yota told me that it was a
misunderstanding.

17:31.633 --> 17:34.261
Yota... She calls him by his first name.

17:35.012 --> 17:39.516
The exams are over, and winter break is
starting, so I'll lose any common ground.

17:45.147 --> 17:46.523
SLURRRP

17:46.607 --> 17:47.983
You possessed or something?

17:48.067 --> 17:48.942
So what?

17:51.403 --> 17:55.199
If I talk to her the next time I see her,
I wonder how she'll react.

17:56.033 --> 18:00.871
Will it be awkward for her, or will
she keep her distance like she used to?

18:00.954 --> 18:01.955
Hmm.

18:02.623 --> 18:03.582
I don't know...

18:04.374 --> 18:05.209
Hm?

18:06.668 --> 18:07.503
Oh.

18:07.586 --> 18:08.545
THUMP

18:09.296 --> 18:11.465
Uh, hey, uh, Amamiya.

18:14.134 --> 18:16.470
Oh, um, well, I, uh...

18:17.346 --> 18:18.180
Hm?

18:19.181 --> 18:21.058
Um, about yesterday.

18:22.101 --> 18:24.311
I'm sorry for crying when I was
apologizing.

18:25.145 --> 18:26.563
It was so embarrassing.

18:27.940 --> 18:29.274
STUNNED

18:29.358 --> 18:32.236
And I promise, I didn't just cry
because I thought it'd make you

18:32.319 --> 18:33.821
- forgive me or something.
- No.

18:33.904 --> 18:34.738
Huh?

18:35.239 --> 18:38.325
No problem.
Sometimes people just get overwhelmed.

18:38.408 --> 18:40.452
There doesn't have to be a particular
reason.

18:40.536 --> 18:41.995
No need to explain yourself.

18:42.079 --> 18:43.038
Huh?

18:43.122 --> 18:44.331
Does that happen to you?

18:44.414 --> 18:45.249
BLANK STARE

18:46.875 --> 18:48.460
- Of course.
- Huh?

18:48.544 --> 18:51.255
You think I don't get or express human
emotions?

18:51.338 --> 18:52.297
Oops.

18:52.798 --> 18:55.592
Aw, that's so mean! Sniffle, sniffle, sniffle.

18:55.676 --> 18:56.927
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

18:57.010 --> 18:58.137
I am surprised though.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.096
Oh.

18:59.596 --> 19:02.850
Listen, I know I may not look like it,
but I'm just a big softie.

19:04.893 --> 19:05.727
Hmmm...

19:06.520 --> 19:07.646
What's with that look?

19:12.442 --> 19:13.986
That's so mean.

19:18.949 --> 19:20.909
Well, I'm heading that way.

19:21.410 --> 19:22.953
Oh, club stuff?

19:23.036 --> 19:24.037
Yeah.

19:25.205 --> 19:26.039
Good luck then.

19:27.708 --> 19:28.584
Thanks.

19:37.009 --> 19:37.843
Ahhhh.

19:40.179 --> 19:41.180
Wahhhhh!

19:43.348 --> 19:46.185
I think I'm learning to stop assuming so
much.

19:46.268 --> 19:49.771
Like that people won't understand me
or that they'll reject me.

19:51.064 --> 19:51.899
Huh?

19:53.358 --> 19:55.569
Come to my work during winter break! Kay,
thanks!

19:55.652 --> 19:57.905
It feels like something has changed a
little.

19:58.906 --> 19:59.990
Or maybe nothing has.

20:00.073 --> 20:00.991
I'LL TELL YOTA TOO

20:01.867 --> 20:02.951
Too soon to tell.

20:04.161 --> 20:07.289
All I know is winter break starts
tomorrow.

21:39.089 --> 21:42.009
KAWAII CAFÉ, WELCOME, WINTER BREAK FAIR PERIOD: DEC. 24TH THROUGH JAN. 10TH

21:42.092 --> 21:43.510
Miharu! Sora! Been too long!

21:44.970 --> 21:47.014
- Yay!
- Yay!

21:47.097 --> 21:49.558
- So how've you been?
- Haven't seen you guys since graduation.

21:49.641 --> 21:50.475
MEETING UP WITH JR. HIGH FRIENDS FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WHILE

21:50.559 --> 21:52.352
How's high school going?

21:52.436 --> 21:53.729
It's been nice and quiet.

21:54.229 --> 21:55.063
Tell me...

21:55.564 --> 21:57.065
You got boyfriends yet?

21:57.149 --> 21:58.025
No way.

21:58.108 --> 21:59.276
Yeah, same here.

21:59.359 --> 22:00.360
Wow, no hesitation.

22:00.986 --> 22:02.029
I'm so surprised, Miki.

22:02.112 --> 22:04.239
You dated a lot back in junior high.

22:04.323 --> 22:07.326
Like that hot upperclassman and the
volleyball player from another school.

22:07.409 --> 22:08.243
Ugh!

22:09.745 --> 22:13.623
Guys would just come on strong
and confess their feelings...

22:13.707 --> 22:15.459
AN UPPERCLASSMAN WITH NO CONNECTION

22:17.919 --> 22:18.754
we'd start dating.

22:18.837 --> 22:21.089
Then, later, they'd break up with me,
saying I wasn't the person that

22:21.173 --> 22:22.758
they thought I was. Every time.

22:24.009 --> 22:24.843
Grr!

22:24.926 --> 22:28.055
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am, then get mad when I

22:28.138 --> 22:29.139
don't live up to it.

22:29.222 --> 22:31.141
Whoa, she switched to gorilla mode.

22:31.224 --> 22:32.434
Sorry I mentioned it.

22:33.185 --> 22:36.521
So I guess in the end I really can't
technically say I dated them.

22:37.356 --> 22:40.442
I promise you, though, the next
time I date someone, I wanna be

22:40.525 --> 22:46.073
the one to confess my feelings to
the person I like before we start dating.

22:46.156 --> 22:48.450
- Anyone in mind?
- Nobody.

22:49.743 --> 22:50.869
What about Amamiya?

22:51.411 --> 22:54.289
I guess things would get awkward
if I asked that now.

22:54.831 --> 22:55.999
- And you, Koyuki?
- Huh?

22:56.083 --> 22:57.292
Do you have a boyfriend?

22:59.169 --> 23:00.003
A boyfriend?

23:04.257 --> 23:05.258
Don't need one.

23:06.593 --> 23:09.596
Plus I don't really think I can
handle dating, to be honest.

23:10.597 --> 23:13.558
So I think it's amazing that you two
have been with your boyfriends

23:13.642 --> 23:14.476
for so long.

23:15.811 --> 23:17.479
Ah, it's not that big a deal.

23:18.397 --> 23:20.273
Do you have any pictures or anything?

23:21.525 --> 23:22.359
Sure, wanna see?

23:24.361 --> 23:26.405
Well, I gotta head to work now.

23:26.488 --> 23:27.489
See ya!

23:27.572 --> 23:29.366
- Bye-bye!
- Let's hang again soon.

23:31.410 --> 23:32.869
- I think she's making things more
- Hm?

23:32.953 --> 23:34.538
Complicated than they are.

23:34.621 --> 23:38.125
Well, don't forget about that whole
Igarashi thing.

23:39.042 --> 23:42.629
Yeah, but to be completely honest,
I've never really understood why she

23:42.712 --> 23:46.007
ever dated him in the first place.

23:47.175 --> 23:48.885
Like, I thought she hated his guts.

23:48.969 --> 23:50.387
Oh my gosh, right?! So I'm not the

23:50.470 --> 23:52.472
- only one who didn't get it!
- That whole thing...

23:52.556 --> 23:54.182
Was probably my fault.
